@@ -15,3 +15,17 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Privacy audit
+
+- Sign-in/sign-up collect only username and password. An adjacent notice identifies the external demo service and explains the purpose, connection metadata, and browser-storage behavior. Use fabricated credentials.
+- Auth requests use HTTPS POST with only those fields, omit cookies and referrers, bypass cache, and reject redirects. The UI ignores response bodies (including tokens and raw errors) and clears passwords after requests finish. Native POST prevents a pre-hydration submission from putting credentials in a URL. Password-manager autocomplete remains available.
+- The shared layout no longer loads analytics, advertising, Google Fonts, or external font preconnections. Typography uses system fonts, and the inactive fireplace ad integration has been removed from the layout.
+- Documents declare UTF-8 and `no-referrer`. Middleware also sends `Referrer-Policy: no-referrer` and disables camera, microphone, and geolocation. Auth pages send `Cache-Control: no-store` and `X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow`, with matching robots metadata.
+- Browsing no longer creates an empty reading-list session. Reading-list writes remain explicit user actions.
+
+Scope limits: the external auth backend is not in this repository, so its credential storage, logging, retention, deletion, and anti-enumeration behavior cannot be verified here. No persistent auth session is implemented. External article images and deliberate DevTools article experiments (including oversized cookies) remain; the privacy notice discloses them. This is an application audit, not a claim of legal compliance.
+
+Verification: `node --test tests/privacy.test.mjs` checks the mocked auth request boundary and shared layout. `pnpm run build` compiles the application. These checks do not contact the authentication service or start a server.
+
+Reference: [MDN Referrer-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Referrer-Policy) and [RequestInit](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/RequestInit).
